    "lawCode": "Amd §4405, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4530\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the education law, in relation to\nreimbursement methodologies for tuition\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis legislation will require the commissioners of education and\nsocial services to develop separate reimbursement methodologies for\ntuition and maintenance of approved private schools and special act\nschool districts.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection two of the bill amends education law section 4405 (4) to\nprovide that the commissioner of education and the commissioner of\nsocial services shall develop reimbursement methodologies for the\ntuition and maintenance components of approved private schools and\nspecial act school districts.\n\nSection two establishes the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\n\"Special Act School Districts\" are public school districts created by\nspecial action of the legislature for the purpose of providing\neducation and related services to students with disabilities-physical,\nemotional and/or mental. Approved private schools also provide\neducation and related services to this student population.\n\nCurrent law requires the commissioners of education and social\nservices to establish one methodology to calculate tuition and\nmaintenance rates for Special Act public schools and private schools.\nThis is significant since public schools, including Special Acts, have\nadditional public school expenses that nonpublic schools do not.\n\nThis bill will allow these agencies to develop separate methodologies\nfor tuition and maintenance rates for the Special Act public schools\nand the nonpublic school districts. This will allow for appropriate\npublic school expenses incurred by Special Act schools to be included\nin these rates.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
