    "lawCode": "Amd §4405, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4530A\n\nSPONSOR: MURPHY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to reimbursement method-\nologies for tuition\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation will require the commissioners of education to develop\nseparate reimbursement methodologies for tuition and maintenance of\napproved private schools and special act school districts.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends education law section 4405 (4) to provide\nthat the commissioner of education shall develop reimbursement methodol-\nogies for the tuition and maintenance components of approved private\nschools and special act school districts.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\n\"Special Act School Districts\" are public school districts created by\nspecial action of the legislature for the purpose of providing education\nand related services to students with disabilities-physical, emotional\nand/or mental. Approved private schools also provide education and\nrelated services to this student population.\n\nCurrent law requires the commissioners of education to establish one\nmethodology to calculate tuition and maintenance rates for Special Act\npublic schools and private schools. This is significant since public\nschools, including Special Acts, have additional public school expenses\nthat nonpublic schools do not.\n\nThis bill will allow these agencies to develop separate methodologies\nfor tuition and maintenance rates for the Special Act public schools and\nthe nonpublic school districts. This will allow for appropriate public\nschool expenses incurred by Special Act schools to be included in these\nrates.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
